Man or beast.

2
00:11:36,923 --> 00:11:42,923
Nightmare Alley is a crime, drama, thriller film directed by Guillermo del Toro.

3
00:17:25,384 --> 00:17:31,384
An ambitious carnival man with a talent for manipulating people with a few well-chosen words
hooks up with a female psychologist who is even more dangerous than he is.

4
00:23:13,846 --> 00:23:19,846
Stanton Carlisle, played by Bradley Cooper.

5
00:29:02,307 --> 00:29:08,307
Dr. Lilith Ritter, played by Cate Blanchett.

6
00:34:50,769 --> 00:34:56,769
Zeena the Seer, played by Toni Collette.

7
00:40:39,230 --> 00:40:45,230
Clem Hoatley, played by Willem Dafoe.

8
00:46:27,692 --> 00:46:33,692
Ezra Grindle, played by Richard Jenkins.

9
00:52:16,153 --> 00:52:22,153
Molly Cahill, played by Rooney Mara.

10
00:58:04,615 --> 00:58:10,615
Nightmare Alley is a 2021 neo-noir psychological thriller film co-written and directed by Guillermo
del Toro, and based on the 1946 novel of the same name by William Lindsay Gresham.

11
01:03:53,076 --> 01:03:59,076
It is the second feature film adaptation of
Gresham's novel, following the 1947 film.

12
01:09:41,538 --> 01:09:47,538
A co-production between Searchlight Pictures and Double Dare You Productions, the film stars Bradley Cooper as a
charming and ambitious carnival worker with a mysterious past who takes big risks to boost his career.

13
01:15:30,000 --> 01:15:36,000
Cate Blanchett, Toni Collette, Willem Dafoe, Richard Jenkins, Rooney Mara,
Ron Perlman, Mary Steenburgen, and David Strathairn also star.

14
01:21:18,461 --> 01:21:24,461
Del Toro announced the film in 2017, and he produced the film alongside J.

15
01:27:06,923 --> 01:27:12,923
Miles Dale and Cooper.

16
01:32:55,384 --> 01:33:01,384
Frequent collaborator Dan Laustsen was the cinematographer, and Nathan
Johnson replaced Alexandre Desplat as its composer.

17
01:38:43,846 --> 01:38:49,846
Principal photography began in January 2020 in Toronto, Ontario, but was
shut down in March 2020 due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

18
01:44:32,307 --> 01:44:38,307
Production resumed in September 2020 and concluded that December.

19
01:50:20,769 --> 01:50:26,769
Nightmare Alley premiered at Alice Tully Hall in New York City on December 1, 2021, and was
theatrically released in the United States on December 17, 2021, by Searchlight Pictures.

20
01:56:09,230 --> 01:56:15,230
It received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised Del Toro’s direction, the cinematography, score,
production design, and performances of Cooper and Blanchett, while criticizing the film's runtime.

21
02:01:57,692 --> 02:02:03,692
The film flopped at the box office, grossing a total of $39.6 million
worldwide against a $60 million production budget.

22
02:07:46,153 --> 02:07:52,153
It received four nominations at the 94th Academy Awards, including Best Picture.

23
02:13:34,615 --> 02:13:40,615
A black-and-white version subtitled Vision in Darkness and Light was
released in select cities starting on January 14, 2022.

24
02:19:23,076 --> 02:19:29,076
The film explores themes of infidelity, based on novel or
book, love triangle, tarot cards, mentor.

25
02:25:11,538 --> 02:25:17,538
The tone is intense and dark and emotional.
